<speak>Plain language and a clear purpose, noted. We can also keep routine scheduling separate from document notifications where possible, so you are not hunting for an appointment inside a message that appears to be about something else. It may help to create a general personal-administration folder in your own mailbox, but there is no need to work on that while we are on the call. You have already spent plenty of time on practical details today. We can leave the technical setup for another occasion and make sure the rest of this conversation stays orderly. I am still hearing you clearly, by the way.</speak>